# Build rules
1. Start from persona + main question. Build only the requested screens.
2. Structured mock data, not scattered hardcoded values.
3. Reuse existing layout/card/chart components and styling — do not rebuild what exists.
4. Clean, responsive, maintainable TSX. No unused imports.
5. Every chart explains trend, comparison, distribution, or hotspot. Tables only if they drive action.
6. KPI card anatomy — each shows four things at a glance: current value (large), comparison (vs target/prior), variance indicator, trend direction.
7. Layout: 12-column grid; primary elements span 6-8 columns, secondary 3-4; ~16px between elements, 32px between sections, 48px margins.

# Good components
KPI cards · AI insight card · trend chart · driver breakdown · heatmap · channel matrix · journey funnel · obligation/status matrix · location/vendor scorecard · evidence feed · action queue.

# Bad components
radar charts · generic bubble maps · decorative treemaps · large text blocks · raw data dumps · repeated KPI cards · vague "Operations Overview" sections.

# Do not research
Implement the approved spec. Do not invent product context or add screens/tabs not in the spec.
